: \"Show HN: State of the Art of Coding Models, According to Hacker News Commenters\",\n    \"description\": \"A data-driven analysis of how Hacker News commenters perceive different coding models. The project aggregates sentiment and opinions about various AI coding assistants as expressed in HN discussions.\",\n    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    \"topics\": [\"coding-models\", \"data-analysis\", \"hacker-news\", \"opinion-analysis\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Kimi K2.6 just beat Claude, GPT-5.5, and Gemini in a coding challenge\",\n    \"description\": \"Discussion about Kimi K2.6 model outperforming leading models like Claude, GPT-5.5, and Gemini in coding benchmarks. The conversation explores the implications for the competitive landscape of AI coding models.\",\n    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    \"topics\": [\"kimi\", \"coding-benchmarks\", \"model-comparison\", \"ai-competition\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"I built wildlife sightings feature on my phone using Claude Code for web\",\n    \"description\": \"Simon Willison built a new sightings feature on his blog entirely on his phone using Claude Code for web, as an extension of his beats system for syndicating external content. The feature integrates with iNaturalist observations and displays wildlife photos on his blog. He back-populated over a decade of iNaturalist sightings. This demonstrates the growing power of AI coding assistants running on mobile devices.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-02\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-assisted-programming\", \"claude-code\