ent\">Improvement</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Copilot Cloud Agent</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Performance improvement: Copilot cloud agent starts 20% faster when using GitHub Actions custom images.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">April 27, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type policy\">Policy</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Copilot Code Review Pricing</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Copilot code review will start consuming GitHub Actions minutes starting June 1, 2026, changing the pricing model for code review features.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">April 27, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://codeium.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Windsurf Next Prerelease</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Launch of Windsurf Next, an opt-in prerelease version of the Windsurf Editor with new features and improvements.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">May 4, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://codeium.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Windsurf Model Updates</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Added support for DeepSeek R1, DeepSeek V3, and OpenAI o3-mini models in Windsurf Editor.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">May 4, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type bugfix\">Bugfix</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code v2.1.123</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Hotfix for OAuth authentication failing with 401 retry loop when experimental betas are disabled.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">April 29, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code v2.1.122</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Added Bedrock service tier support, PR URL paste feature for /resume, enhanced MCP management UI, and multiple fixes for Vertex AI, Bedrock, and OAuth connectivity issues.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">April 28, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Column (25%) -->\n            <section class=\"column technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n                <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights (13)</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47976415\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Uber torches 2026 AI budget</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Massive discussion revealing 95% of Uber engineers use AI tools monthly with 70% of committed code from AI. Monthly API costs per engineer ranged from $500-$2,000, far exceeding budget projections.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Hacker News</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">enterprise-ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px; font-size: 11px;\">\n                        <strong>Key:</strong> Tokenmaxxing concerns, context management importance, productivity measurement debates\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildlife sightings via phone</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison built a wildlife sightings feature entirely on his phone using Claude Code for web, integrating with iNaturalist observations and back-populating a decade of sightings.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">mobile-dev</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI /goal feature</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Codex CLI 0.128.0 adds /goal - agentic looping until completion using the Ralph loop: keeps looping until goal achieved or token budget exhausted.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Specsmaxxing - YAML specs</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Discussion about YAML-based specifications for AI systems, touching on how teams approach AI development and importance of proper specification with AI coding assistants.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Hacker News</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">yaml</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">specifications</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">VS Code Copilot attribution</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub issue about VS Code automatically adding 'Co-Authored-by Copilot' to commits regardless of usage. Large discussion on attribution, consent, and automatic AI attribution.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Hacker News</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ethics</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">attribution</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zig's anti-LLM policy</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Zig's stringent anti-LLM policy values contributors over contributions. LLM assistance breaks their investment model in growing trusted contributors. Why review LLM code vs firing up your own LLM?\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Agent harness architecture</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Discussion about whether agent harnesses should run inside or outside sandboxed environments, touching on security, performance, and architectural patterns for agentic AI.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Hacker News</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">architecture</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kimi K2.6 beats Claude/GPT</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Kimi K2.6 model outperforms leading models like Claude, GPT-5.5, and Gemini in coding benchmarks. Discussion explores implications for competitive landscape.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Hacker News</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">benchmarks</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UK AI Security: GPT-5.5 eval</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        UK's AI Security Institute evaluated GPT-5.5 for finding security vulnerabilities, found it comparable to Claude Mythos but generally available now.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-security</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Andrew Kelley: LLM 'smell'</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Zig creator explains LLM-generated code has a 'digital smell' - LLM hallucinations differ fundamentally from human mistakes. 'I'm not telling you not to smoke, but don't smoke in my house.'\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">opinion</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">zig</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RSS for vibe-coded apps</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Matt Webb argues vibe-coding makes apps more personal and frequent. Shipping tools becomes like blog posts. Simon added Atom feed to his tools page.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">rss</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Show HN: Coding models sentiment</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Data-driven analysis of how Hacker News commenters perceive different coding models. Aggregates sentiment and opinions about AI coding assistants from HN discussions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Hacker News</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">data-analysis</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microsoft VibeVoice</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Whisper-style audio model with speaker diarization, MIT licensed. Transcribed hour-long podcast in 8:45 on 128GB M5 Max, using 30GB RAM at peak.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">speech-to-text</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a> |\n                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Whitelist Updates</a> |\n                <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a>\n            </p>\n            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\n                Agentic Coding Research Report • Generated on May 4, 2026 • Hacker News-inspired design\n            </p>\n        </div>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}

